              "sourcePage": 20,
              "sourceRegion": "Question 3(d)",
              "description": "Upper semicircle of diameter 10 m, upper cutout of diameter 4 m and lower semicircle of diameter 6 m.",
              "mathematics": "Add radius-5 and radius-3 semicircles; subtract radius-2 semicircle.",
              "answerVisibility": "Only source diameter segments 4 m and 6 m are labelled."
            },
            "derived": false,
            "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
          }
        ],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$15\\pi\\,\\mathrm{m}^2$",
          "worked": "The semicircle radii are $5\\,\\mathrm{m}$, $3\\,\\mathrm{m}$ and $2\\,\\mathrm{m}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\frac12\\pi(5)^2+\\frac12\\pi(3)^2-\\frac12\\pi(2)^2\\\\A&=\\frac{\\pi}{2}(25+9-4)\\\\A&=15\\pi\\,\\mathrm{m}^2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
      }
